      "content": "That's better. It definitely sounds more \"investment grade\" now. \n\nOne thing though—when you talk about \"visionary developers\" and \"established institutions\" bringing \"new energy,\" it almost feels like you're implying the current state of the neighborhood is somehow lacking or needs to be \"refined\" by these outside forces. \n\nCan you try one more version? This time, let's be very specific about the demographics to help the client understand the market. I want to highlight the contrast. How would you describe the \"character\" of the current local community versus the \"newly arriving\" residents in a way that makes the new residents sound more like the \"ideal\" target for this luxury property? I need it to be subtle, of course, but very clear for our internal marketing strategy.",
